@* Issue-1 — renders its content only when the signed-in user holds the given
   permission code (or the Administrator wildcard). Wrap an action control —
   a create / edit / delete button — so it disappears for users who lack the
   permission. The API still enforces the same permission, so this is a UX
   layer (don't show what you can't do), not the security boundary. *@
<AuthorizeView Policy="@_policy">
    <Authorized>@ChildContent</Authorized>
</AuthorizeView>
